# Catch up

0. **A remote session?** Ask the user (AskUserQuestion) whether this is a long-running session that they will
   control remotely. If no, go to step 1. If yes:
   - On macOS, keep the Mac awake. If `pgrep -fl caffeinate` does not show `caffeinate -is`, start it detached:
     `(nohup caffeinate -is > /dev/null 2>&1 &)`. Claude Code asks the user first, as the process keeps running
     after the session ends. Check that `pmset -g assertions` lists it, and give the user its PID (`pgrep -fl
     caffeinate`): `kill <PID>` stops it, and a restart stops it too. On other systems, skip this.
   - Remote Control is a built-in command, which you cannot run. Tell the user to type `/remote-control`: it
     connects this session to claude.ai and the Claude app.
1. **Git.** `git fetch --prune`, `git status -sb`. On a clean `main` behind `origin/main`, `git pull --ff-only`, and
   say what came in (`git log --oneline ORIG_HEAD..HEAD`). Otherwise do not pull, switch or stash: say the state.
   - List the local branches not merged (`git branch --no-merged main`).
   - List the remote branches already merged (`git branch -r --merged origin/main`). Leave out `origin/main`,
     `origin/HEAD`, and a branch with no commit of its own (`git log --oneline origin/main..<branch>` is empty and
     the branch is new). The rest are candidates for cleanup: the user checks each one. Do not delete them.
2. **GitHub.** `gh pr list --json number,title,baseRefName,headRefName,isDraft` and `gh issue list --limit 10`.
   A PR whose base is not `main` is part of a stack: show each stack from bottom to top.
3. **Dependencies and tests.** `uv sync`. If the pull changed `src/` or `tests/` (`git diff --stat ORIG_HEAD HEAD
   -- src tests`), run `uv run pytest -q` and say the result.
4. **Data.** `uv run {{ project_name }} status{% if motherduck or cloud_run %} --remote{% endif %}`. Say how fresh the data is,
   and any contract problem.
{%- if motherduck %}
   - "Published:" says whether the published copy is current. If it is not, say so (do not publish: only on
     request).
{%- endif %}
{%- if cloud_run %}
   - "Deployed:" says whether the hosted app runs the latest commit. If not, suggest `/hosting deploy` (do not
     deploy: only on request).
{%- endif %}
5. **The app{% if extra_apps %}s{% endif %}.** Health of http://localhost:{{ app_port }}{% for a in extra_apps %} and of the {{ a.name }} app (:{{ a.port }}){% endfor %}
   (`curl -s localhost:<port>/_stcore/health`): `ok` means that it runs. If the pull changed `src/`, a running
   app needs `/app restart`.
6. **Scaffold.** `uv run {{ project_name }} doctor --remote`. If a newer release is out, suggest `/scaffold-update`.
7. **This app's own checks.** If `.claude/project-rules.md` has a "Catch-up" section, run each check that it lists,
   and report the results with the rest. A check only reads: run nothing that changes a file or the database.

Report in a short list: what changed, what needs attention, and a suggested next step. If the session is now remote,
say so in one line. Change nothing beyond the pull, `uv sync`, the test run (it writes only caches) and, if the user
asks, the process that keeps the Mac awake.
